# ── Deployment secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The hosted database's connection string and the API's signing key. These are
# live credentials for a publicly reachable deployment: a leaked connection
# string is direct database access, and a leaked signing key lets anyone mint a
# token for any member.
#
# Kept in a file rather than in shell history so they are not re-typed, and
# ignored so they cannot be committed by accident.
.env.deploy
.env.deploy.*

# ── Documentation is not committed ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Reports, matrices, reviews and phase write-ups stay local.
*.md
docs/

# -- ...but two of those are build inputs, not documentation ------------------
#
# Roslyn analyzer release tracking is .md by convention, and
# Diaspora.Analyzers.csproj lists both files as compile inputs. The blanket
# rule above caught them by extension.
#
# They exist in every working tree, so nothing local ever fails. The only
# place it appears is a clean checkout -- CI, a new machine, a release build:
#
#     CSC : error CS2001: Source file AnalyzerReleases.Shipped.md
#           could not be found.
#
# Recorded as UAT-131. Re-inclusion works because the exclusion is on the
# extension, not on a parent directory; git cannot re-include a file whose
# directory is itself excluded, which is why docs/ needs different treatment
# and has not been given one here.
!src/Diaspora.Analyzers/AnalyzerReleases.Shipped.md
!src/Diaspora.Analyzers/AnalyzerReleases.Unshipped.md

# -- ...and a third, which is a test input ------------------------------------
#
# AnalyzerCatalog.md lived in docs/platform until 11 Nov 2026, where
# AnalyzerCatalogTests read it. That test therefore passed on every working
# tree and threw DirectoryNotFoundException on a clean checkout -- it had
# never run, because the analyzer suite was not in CI either. The first CI
# run of that suite is what found it.
#
# It could not be rescued where it stood: docs/ is excluded as a DIRECTORY and
# git cannot re-include a file inside one. Moving it beside the two files
# above puts it back under the extension rule, which is re-includable.
#
# The rule is the one the note above states: a guardrail's input must be in
# the repository, or the guardrail is a comment.
!src/Diaspora.Analyzers/AnalyzerCatalog.md

# -- ...and a fourth, the same rule a third time ------------------------------
#
# AlertCatalog.md is the platform's alert definitions (BARCH-008 step 3), read
# by AlertCatalogArchitectureTests to prove that every alert names an
# instrument that exists, every meter it names is subscribed by a contributor,
# and no instrument documenting itself as worth alerting on has been left out.
#
# It was written into src/Diaspora.Observability/ specifically to avoid the
# docs/ trap above, and the blanket extension rule caught it anyway -- the
# tests passed locally while the file would not have existed on a clean
# checkout, where File.ReadAllText throws rather than skips. Found before the
# commit this time rather than by CI.
!src/Diaspora.Observability/AlertCatalog.md

# -- ...and the decision register, which is the fourth time the same rule -----
#
# The three notes above each end the same way: a guardrail's input must be in
# the repository, or the guardrail is a comment. The architectural decision
# register is the same thing one level up. Twenty-two ADRs recorded why this
# platform is shaped as it is, and not one of them was in a clean checkout --
# invisible to CI, to a new machine, and to anybody who was not the author.
# BARCH-004 asked for its decision to be written into an ADR, which would have
# produced a twenty-third invisible file.
#
# The notes above say a file inside docs/ cannot be rescued, and twice solved
# it by moving the file out. That is right for one build input and wrong for a
# register of twenty-three: re-inclusion works as long as every parent is
# un-excluded first, which is what the three lines below do. docs/* then
# re-excludes everything else under docs/ by name, so the audit reports, the
# phase write-ups and the release-readiness notes stay exactly as local as
# they were.
!docs/
docs/*
!docs/adrs/
!docs/adrs/*.md

.neon
.env.local
node_modules/

# Output of a workstation publish for docker/Dockerfile.prebuilt; never committed.
prebuilt/
